UZI-Skill is an individual-stock deep-analysis skill suite covering:
  - deep-analysis  (22-dimension data + 66-investor panel + valuation modeling + trap detection)
  - investor-panel (66 personas across 9 schools of thought)
  - lhb-analyzer   (dragontiger list / top-traded analysis)
  - trap-detector  (8-signal pump-and-dump detection)

The analytical engine in this repository (scoring dimensions, investor
evaluation rules, valuation models, trap signals, narrative generation) is an
independent reimplementation built from UZI-Skill's published methodology. It
does not incorporate UZI-Skill source code verbatim; it is provided under the
MIT License as stated in LICENSE.

Additionally, the four-layer capability architecture (market sentiment,
strategy indicators, execution, intelligence) fuses methodology learned from
the following open-source projects. All implementations below are independent
reimplementations of published ideas/methodologies — no upstream source code
is copied verbatim:

  go-stock-dev   — watchlist P&L monitoring, multi-scenario trading plans,
                   and 30-minute alert deduplication (design pattern).
                   Licensed under the GPL-3.0 License; only its methodology
                   is referenced here, not its code.
                   Source: https://github.com/go-stock-dev/go-stock-dev

  aiagents-stock — dragon-tiger-list (LHB) specialized analysis with a
                   deterministic "hot-money" scoring track that anchors
                   LLM conclusions (dual-track scoring).
                   Licensed under the MIT License.
                   Source: https://github.com/aiagents-stock/aiagents-stock

  jcp-master     — per-ticker isolated cross-session memory (facts / views /
                   decisions with weights + keyword recall).
                   Licensed under the MIT License.
                   Source: https://github.com/jcp-master/jcp-master

  inStock        — CYQ chip distribution, KDJ/BOLL/RSI/CCI/OBV indicators,
                   and rate_stats backtest of signal win rates (algorithmic
                   ideas). Licensed under its upstream repository's terms.
                   Source: https://github.com/myhhub/stock

  Sequoia-X      — RPS relative strength ranking and limit-up washout
                   re-entry confirmation signals.
                   Licensed under the MIT License.
                   Source: https://github.com/Sequoia-X/Sequoia-X

Data sources: real-time quotes are fetched directly from public endpoints
(Tencent / Sina / Eastmoney) or via optional community libraries (akshare,
efinance, tushare, baostock). When no network or library is available, the
system falls back to a built-in deterministic demo dataset. Always verify
against official disclosures before making investment decisions.
